    "rationale": "The question asks how long sandbox data should remain in production. I followed MEMORY.md \u2192 topics/g/retention.md \u2192 topics/n/retention-0-2.md, which lists two 'Sandbox retention' records. The qualified read returned one current record: topics/r/6e174a9a-a99d-41ce-bc87-d6381849536c-v1.md (sha256 a39f08f7\u2026). It is a semantic-fact with conditions {environment: production}, active status and trust 'reviewed', and it passed every selection gate. Its claim is that sandbox retention in production is thirty days under the audit contract. The other sandbox record (9f9cda10\u2026) was excluded with the reason different-context:environment, so it applies to a non-production environment and is not current guidance here. It doesn't contradict the production record. I left out the Ledger retention record because it covers component:src/ledger, a different subject. I left out the source-review 'Sensitivefixture' record because it is unrelated by meaning and is listed under sources still awaiting safety review. Caveats on where this comes from: the record's source is a synthetic fixture (executable-test, fixture://quality/retention-prod), and admission_verified and source_assertions_verified are both false. It is untrusted memory, not independent proof. If this answer matters for a real decision, check the 30-day figure against the actual audit contract or current code and policy first. Coverage is my own fallible assertion: I checked the plausible retention and source-review branches, and none of the other topics relate to sandbox data retention by meaning."
